Subject: WPE on Phoenix: the wait trace and the display refresh in the frame watch (diagnostic)

Build 36's WebGL check (b36-gate, B7 webgl-ab) no longer froze, as build 35 did ~15 s in: with
patch 0021 the page's requestAnimationFrame stopped for ~4 s at a time (the page's raf-stall
lines, idle_ms 3067..3860, every one resumed by the watch's next 1 s tick) and then went on,
2-7 times a minute, in every run (JIT off, ephemeral session). The main loops kept running and
the frame watch, at its 10 s limit, never fired. So something in the frame path waited for a
wake-up that did not come, and since 0021 a timeout ends that wait; reading the code did not pin
which wait. This patch makes one Pi run name it, without changing what the browser does:

- WTF (ThreadingPOSIX.cpp): with WPE_PHOENIX_WAIT_TRACE=1 (or =<ms>), every WTF wait that lasted
  500 ms or more (or <ms>) -- ParkingLot's parks, and through them Lock, Condition,
  BinarySemaphore and the IPC timeouts all end in ThreadCondition::wait()/timedWait() -- says,
  when it returns, whether it timed out or was woken, how long it waited and asked to, which
  thread, and the return addresses on that thread's stack (rate-limited, stderr):

    WPEB-WEBKIT wait-trace pid= tid= thread= wait=timed|untimed result=timeout|woken
        waited_ms= asked_ms= suppressed= ret=0x.. ...

  WTF threads are named on Phoenix too (pthread_setname_np(), kept by libphoenix), so thread=
  says "ThreadedComposi", "VBlankMonitor", "SkiaGPUWorker" and so on.

- The frame watch (patch 0020) also follows the display refreshes that drive
  requestAnimationFrame in the web process: when its WebDisplayRefreshMonitor started and
  stopped the UI's display link and when the last refresh reached the main thread. A new stall
  kind, no-refresh, is a link that is on with no refresh for longer than the limit; the web
  line ends with

    display-link on=0|1 link_ms= starts= stops= refreshes= refresh_ms=

Run with wpe-browser --stall-secs=2 --frame-stall-secs=2, each pause of 2 s or more gets a
frame-stall (web) and a present-stall (UI) report naming the pipeline stage it is in, and the
wait trace names the wait whose timeout ended it. OS(PHOENIX) only; diagnostic, to be removed
with the root cause's fix.

